# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and local credentials — never tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
secrets/
*.secret
# Backup and runtime artifacts that carry state or secrets (security audit SEC-15).
*.db
*.bundle
*.tar.zst
rendered*.yml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Freqtrade runtime state.
# The runtime config is generated from config.paper.json.example and must never
# be committed: committing it would make the effective config ambiguous.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
freqtrade/user_data/config.json
freqtrade/user_data/config.local.json
freqtrade/user_data/*.sqlite*
freqtrade/user_data/logs/
freqtrade/user_data/plot/
freqtrade/user_data/notebooks/
freqtrade/user_data/hyperopt.lock

# FP-CONTROL-1 forward-paper runtime state. The evidence ledgers are the
# cohort's live evidence lane: they are append-only, they grow for the whole
# window, and a runtime that kept the worktree dirty would trip the protocol's
# own clean-worktree stop condition. They stay on the host and are published
# deliberately as closure artifacts, not swept in by an incidental commit.
freqtrade/user_data/fp-control-1/

# The same, for the one other DECLARED instance lane. A qualification run writes
# ledgers, a database and logs into its lane; left untracked they fail the
# repository's own integrity gate, and the tempting fix — committing them — is
# exactly what must never happen to evidence.
#
# Listed literally, one line per lane the registry actually declares. A prefix
# pattern was tried and withdrawn: `fp-control-*/` also hid `fp-control-3`,
# `fp-control-A` and `fp-control-PRODUCTION`, none of which the registry
# declares. An ignore rule that hides an undeclared lane hides exactly the thing
# an operator most needs to see — a second runtime writing evidence nobody
# authorised — and it hides it from `git status`, which is the signal the
# forward-paper protocol's own clean-worktree stop condition depends on.
freqtrade/user_data/fp-control-2/

# And the successor control the registry now declares. Listed literally for the
# reason stated above: `fp-control-*/` would also hide lanes nobody authorised.
freqtrade/user_data/fp-control-3/

# Disposable lanes built by the adversarial tests, and nothing else.
# `lane.resolve_lane` insists a lane root live under this directory, so a test
# that exercises archival has nowhere else to build one, and a test that fails
# mid-run would otherwise leave the worktree dirty. The namespace is deliberately
# one that can never name a real instance: the registry's role enum is closed to
# FP-CONTROL-1/2 and FP-CANDIDATE-A/B, so no declared lane can ever be called
# `fp-testlane-…`, and tests/test_p2_gitignore_boundary.py asserts that.
freqtrade/user_data/fp-testlane-*/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Market data and derived artifacts.
# Datasets are reproduced via scripts/download_data.sh and pinned by
# research/datasets/*.lock.json — the payload itself stays out of Git.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
freqtrade/user_data/data/
freqtrade/user_data/backtest_results/
freqtrade/user_data/hyperopt_results/
freqtrade/user_data/models/
freqtrade/user_data/freqaimodels/
*.feather
*.parquet

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Experiment tracking runtime state (MLflow keeps its own store).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
mlruns/
mlartifacts/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Host-run evidence outputs.
# The activation pack writes its run evidence here — the acquisition manifest,
# the dataset audit, preflight and admission reports, and the closure pack.
# They are regenerated on every run and would keep the worktree permanently
# dirty during a forward-paper window, which is the protocol's own S2 stop
# condition. Classified, not discarded (CLOUD-0 C0.2): the files stay on the
# host, and closure evidence is published deliberately rather than swept in by
# an incidental commit.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
artifacts/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local research records are evidence, but only the ones deliberately committed
# under research/records/ belong in Git. Scratch runs stay local.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
research/records/scratch/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python / tooling.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# External benchmark sprint: upstream sources are pinned by hash and fetched on
# demand, never committed. Two pinned projects are GPL-3.0 and three carry no
# license at all, so this directory must stay out of the tree.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.upstream-cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Archives and OS noise.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Research configs generated by merging the paper example with an overlay.
freqtrade/user_data/config.research.json
